[h1]TVM Network Tuner — BETA[/h1]

An optional Project Zomboid Build 42 companion for Trader Vending Machines that suppresses automatic visual-synchronization polling.

[b]Version:[/b] 0.2.0-beta
[b]Target:[/b] Project Zomboid Build 42
[b]Tested with:[/b] Project Zomboid 42.21.0

[h2]What it does[/h2]
This addon blocks only TVM's automatic visual registry and snapshot polling by default. Normal machine UI, purchases, owner actions, placement, and TVM persistence remain under TVM's existing authority.

[h2]Features[/h2]
- Event-driven visual synchronization with a server-side guard.
- TVM's existing deduplicated map-marker refresh after successful state changes.
- Sandbox-controlled pass-through mode and low-volume diagnostics.

[h2]Current status[/h2]
This is a BETA build. It has run on a live dedicated server since August 2026 without an addon-related issue, and diagnostic logs confirm automatic visual-request suppression and state-change hooks. Bandwidth savings have not been measured in bytes, and removing the addon from an existing world has not yet been tested. Back up a live world before changing its mod list; do not use this addon to remove TVM or repair existing TVM save data.

[h2]Configuration[/h2]
[code]
TVMPerformance.TrafficControlEnabled=true
TVMPerformance.EventDrivenVisualSync=true
TVMPerformance.DiagnosticsEnabled=false
[/code]

Traffic control defaults to enabled, event-driven mode defaults to enabled, and diagnostics default to disabled. Restart the server and reconnect clients after changing addon sandbox settings.

[h2]Server setup[/h2]
[code]
WorkshopItems=3793134223
Mods=pz-tvm-fix
[/code]

Install the same addon build with TVM on the server and participating clients.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
Requires Trader Vending Machines on Project Zomboid Build 42. Tested on a dedicated server with Project Zomboid 42.21.0 and the TVM Workshop release dated 2026-04-20. If an issue occurs, set traffic control to false, restart, and reconnect before considering addon removal.

[h2]Source code, documentation, and issues[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/jonathanjacobs/pz-tvm-fix]GitHub — TVM Network Tuner repository[/url]

See the repository for installation, test procedures, observed evidence, limitations, and issue reporting.

